{"id":"n-20261009-x9kctd","category":"sports","display_title":"Fifa Leadership Contest Shifts","display_title_he":"שינויים במרוץ להנהגת פיפ\"א","short_summary":"Victor Montagliani will run again for Concacaf rather than challenging Gianni Infantino, while Uefa's Aleksander Ceferin seeks another term and pushes for extensive reforms.","english_level":"C1","words":547,"reading_time":4,"image":null,"sources":[{"name":"BBC Sport","domain":"bbc.co.uk","url":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/articles/cmn4ex2y53l8o","title":"Infantino given re-election boost as Montagliani seeks final Concacaf term","published_at":"2026-10-08T20:09:46.000Z"},{"name":"The Guardian","domain":"theguardian.com","url":"https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/oct/08/victor-montagliani-concacaf-reelection-fifa-presidency","title":"Victor Montagliani eyes re-election at Concacaf that would rule out Fifa presidency run","published_at":"2026-10-08T16:00:23.000Z"}],"published_at":"2026-10-08T16:00:23.000Z","first_published_in_app_at":"2026-10-09T06:31:28.283Z","quality_score":9,"interest_score":8,"verification_status":"verified","content_status":"published","paragraphs":["The landscape of international football administration has shifted significantly as potential challengers clarify their intentions ahead of upcoming presidential elections. Victor Montagliani, the 61-year-old head of Concacaf, has indicated to colleagues and staff during a town hall meeting that he will seek a final term leading the confederation governing North and Central America and the Caribbean, rather than mounting a challenge for the top job at Fifa. The Canadian official had previously been viewed by European member associations as a strong potential candidate to oppose incumbent Gianni Infantino, especially following widespread international backlash over a controversial proposal to sell stakes in the World Cup to private investors. The upcoming presidential election for Concacaf will take place in the first quarter of next year, immediately preceding the Fifa vote scheduled for March 18 in Rabat. Montagliani previously took office a decade ago on a reforming mandate following a major corruption scandal and subsequent FBI investigation that resulted in the arrest of his predecessor, Jeffrey Webb, who admitted to taking bribes and kickbacks.","With Montagliani stepping aside from a potential presidential run against Infantino, European football governing body Uefa faces mounting pressure to identify a unifying alternative before the candidate registration deadline of November 18. Meanwhile, Uefa president Aleksander Ceferin confirmed to delegates during a meeting of all 55 national association chiefs in Berlin that he will stand for a fourth term in office. Ceferin's announcement reverses his earlier insistence from February 2024 that he would step down, though a rule change regarding his initial tenure—which began in September 2016 and did not count toward the standard limit—has paved the way for his continued leadership for more than 15 years in total. Ceferin expressed gratitude to the national associations for their trust and stated his ambition to keep European football united. While ruling out a personal run against Infantino, he remains committed to finding a respected, unifying figure rooted in football to contest the March election. As yet, no confirmed candidate has emerged, though former Tottenham Hotspur and Switzerland defender Ramon Vega has stated his intention to run, even as doubts remain regarding whether he can secure the five letters of support required to appear on the ballot paper.","In tandem with these developments, Ceferin and Uefa have intensified their campaign for structural changes within world football's governing body following the Fifa Forward Enterprise sell-off scandal. Uefa published a comprehensive 14-point reform plan designed to curtail certain direct executive powers held by the Fifa president, safeguard independent oversight bodies such as ethics and disciplinary committees from institutional interference, and ensure that institutional resources are never utilized for personal or electoral advantage. Furthermore, the reform framework demands that at least ten million dollars of additional funding should be made available to each of the 211 member associations, alongside a portion of Fifa's six billion dollar cash reserves. Although Uefa, Concacaf, and the Asian Football Confederation previously issued open letters accusing Infantino of breaking trust through deception, AFC President Sheikh Salman bin Ibrahim Al Khalifa has recently softened his stance. Leadership figures from these confederations are expected to press for independent reviews and broader reforms during upcoming council meetings in Zurich, even as nations like Azerbaijan maintain divergent positions, with the Azeri FA outlier maintaining close ties to Fifa through chief member associations officer Elkhan Mammadov."],"facts":[{"fact":"Victor Montagliani intends to seek a final term as president of Concacaf, ruling him out of running for the Fifa presidency.","sources":[1,2]},{"fact":"Gianni Infantino is seeking a fourth term as Fifa president in March's election.","sources":[1,2]},{"fact":"Aleksander Ceferin will stand for a fourth term as Uefa president, announcing his decision at a meeting in Berlin.","sources":[1,2]},{"fact":"Uefa published a 14-point reform plan for Fifa and is searching for a unifying candidate to challenge Infantino by November 18.","sources":[1]}],"glossary":[{"text":"landscape","lemma":"landscape","pos":"noun","he":"נוף, מפה","name":false},{"text":"international","lemma":"international","pos":"adjective","he":"בינלאומי","name":false},{"text":"football","lemma":"football","pos":"noun","he":"כדורגל","name":false},{"text":"administration","lemma":"administration","pos":"noun","he":"ניהול, מינהל","name":false},{"text":"shifted","lemma":"shift","pos":"verb","he":"השתנה, זז","name":false},{"text":"significantly","lemma